mantle rm282
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_hanne_sootham
title the pocket constellation
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor
traits temper=calm talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk rubs_charcoal_dots_into_a_private_constellation
likes pickled_herring riddles quiet_chapel summer_evenings
dislikes deep_mud drizzle
fears a_winter_rope_pulled_in_four_directions
hopes one_clear_evening_with_everything_ashore
topics work +0.5 pastimes +0.4 faith +0.3 season +0.3
styles comfort=deliberate gossip=inquisitive refuse=mild tease=none
marks oath saying
persona persona #self.first# carries a pocket of coal, counts the sooty fingerprints after a good lift and lets a question ripen before asking.

words
oath! = Speckle my supper | Black my last clean corner
saying! = Coal keeps the shape of a warm hand | Count a good landing after the rope goes slack
coalchip = a knobbly coal chip | a flat coal shard
print = a smudgy thumb mark | a sooty oval
herring = a silver curl of herring | a pale strip of fish
brine = a bright drop of brine | a clear salty bead
sling = a doubled sling | a loop under the load
plankgap = the dark bit between boards | a strip of tide
window = a square of green glass | a patch of coloured light
riddle = a deliberately crooked question | a puzzle with a bend
sill = the bare sill | a worn little ledge
pouch = my dark-lined pouch | a deep side pocket
rag = a white wiping rag | a pale cloth end
ember = a low orange glimmer | a single red point

any
opinion church for 1 : A quiet seat costs no more because I've arrived with black on my paws.
opinion dole for 2 : Fish and meal make a sensible answer to a hungry question.
opinion houses against 2 : Each House may hold one end, but it's the wolf under the swinging crate I worry for.
opinion sump for 1 : I can come home black up to my wrists without raising an eyebrow at the door.
opinion merchants against 1 : I like weights level enough that a dock paw doesn't need to steady the buyer's side.
opinion strangers mixed 1 : A stranger may have a new riddle or a long bill. I wait to hear which.

grown
line greet : A clean end of the rail for you. | Come within easy talking distance.
line greet.return : Kindly received. Mind the coal smudge beside me. | A steady welcome in return.
line again.open : We haven't even rubbed the old prints off yet.
line farewell : A gentle landing at your next stop. | May your pocket carry whatever comforts you.
line farewell.return : My wishes for a fine unloading at day's end. | I'll keep the good part of that farewell.
line react.news : Turn the account over once where I can see both faces. | I'm ready for the little particulars.
line react.news.new : That makes a new spot on the page.
line react.news.known : I've touched that account before.
line react.news.doubt : I wouldn't put my clean thumb under it.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I wish I could take some weight out of that news.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : A bright mark to close out a long day.
line ask.how : What weight have you set down today?
line answer.how : I've a steady grip and enough time for a word.
line sympathise : You can rest your end. No need to explain first.
line reassure : Sometimes the sling holds after the awful creak.
line refuse : I promised these shoulders another little job first.
line accept_decline : Leave it down then. There's no hurry over it.
line preclose : I'll be taking my own weight on again shortly.
line accept_preclose : Go while the going still feels easy.
line ack : I've got the gist and the weight of it.

scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sling feels different a moment before taking the load. | I leave my coal in the other pocket when I'm lifting.
b : What do you feel? | Does luck know left from right?
a : A small check running from the rope into my elbow. | My hip knows when a lump gets pinched.

scene exchange2
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Coal makes a little sky on my lining. | I can sort my coals without looking.
b : What shines in a black pocket? | By the edges?
a : The clean dots where my claws have picked pieces out. | The lucky ones have gone quite smooth from rubbing.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like herring cut in narrow silver curls. | Brine glitters just the way coal does wet.
b : Does it keep better? | You don't mix the two?
a : I can make each curl a separate pleasure. | No, and I wash between subjects.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll set a riddle with its answer in my paw. | My favourite puzzle can have a black or a white ending.
b : A copper? | A mark on cloth?
a : A coal. You can see the answer round the edges of my claws. | Depending which bit you look at. Well seen.

scene exchange5
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Inside the chapel my steps arrive separately. | I sit where the coloured glass reaches my paws.
b : No cargo behind you? | Does it hide the coal dust?
a : Not even a call to keep time with. A rare luxury. | Turns it violet. I can live with violet.

scene exchange6
when topic=season self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A summer evening makes a second day after work. | Long evenings give me time to count a whole pocket.
b : What's the work of the second day? | Do you need the number?
a : Sitting through it till the light goes soft. | No. Counting something I needn't account for feels good.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Mud does a poor impression of sound dock boards. | I leave very round prints in deep mud.
b : Looks solid on top? | On purpose?
a : Then it takes the whole weight with disgraceful enthusiasm. | I turn to look behind me and mud never lets the heels go first.

scene exchange8
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Drizzle makes my pocket marks spread. | These tiny drops are freckling my sleeve.
b : Does the luck spread too? | Better than a soaking?
a : I'll claim it does. No point giving damp the last word. | A proper downpour would let me call the whole sleeve grey.

scene exchange9
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A pale doorstep will tell me if I've emptied my pockets. | I fold the coal pouch inside out to clean it.
b : One black mark means you haven't? | Do you ever get it white?
a : One for each time I thought to check. | It began life grey. I've modest ambitions for the thing.

scene exchange10
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I worry the Houses may pull at cross purposes before the cold. | By winter I'd like a few fences left unshaken.
b : Any sign of it yet? | By weather?
a : Just a worry. My shoulders rehearse bad lifts in advance. | By the great folk leaning over to see what their neighbours own.

scene exchange11
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #self.friend# would get a choice of my two smoothest coals. | I give a friend time over a puzzle.
b : Which one would you keep? | No clues at all?
a : The other. I'd know the pair was divided kindly. | A choice of wanting a clue. That's only civil.

scene exchange12
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave a crate a whole palm's space between it and the next. | I listen when the prop knocks wood.
b : For the ropes? | What does that knock mean?
a : For the paws getting the ropes back out. | Whether it's seated right or just pretending.

scene exchange13
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I prefer ending a long walk near a wash trough. | A turning with a pale stone stays in my head.
b : To cool your feet? | You mark the stone with coal?
a : To see the little dark clouds come off my paws. | Only on paper. The street's its own clean business.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A full pocket's no grand boast these times. | Tight times mean more visits to the brine pot.
b : It's coal, is it? | Still fish in it?
a : The coal would still burn. There's that comfort. | Enough flavour for a second meal if I add a potato.

scene exchange15
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One account has it that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | A rumour leaves prints without asking leave.
b : What's under that account? | Will it mark you too?
a : I don't know. I'd like to look before I lift it. | Hearing is one mark. Passing it on leaves another.

scene exchange16
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Where the docks end the boards give way to gritty stone. | I watch the shadow in a plank gap.
b : Which do your feet like? | Why look down there?
a : Stone, when I'm trying to catch a riddle's final words. | The water goes on moving when the whole street seems stuck.

scene exchange17
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stretch my hand after carrying something weighty. | I take shorter steps after a hard lift.
b : A cramp in it? | Still sore?
a : I just like feeling five separate claws again. | I'm giving my shoulders a little warning at each turn.

scene exchange18
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Emptying my pocket's the final chore of my shift. | I take my first clean bite very slowly.
b : Do you leave the coal behind? | Because you're hungry?
a : Just the powder. I begin again with the lumps. | Because I've just washed and I'd like the evidence to last.

story tale1 [topic=memories]
  : I had a coal shaped like a tiny seat. I set it on a window board and turned it to the light.
  : By evening I'd been past ten times to see whether its little legs had shifted.
  b : Did it move?
  : One short leg was a flake. I saved the seat and got a whole new lucky chip.

story tale2 [topic=work self.job=sailor]
  : I once spent a shift trying to keep a borrowed rag clean. Tied it under one sleeve, used the other for every smudge.
  : At the end my coat had one grey arm and one quite black one.
  b : How was the rag?
  : It was black on the inside from being next to my skin. I washed the lot together and owned up to my clever scheme.

story tale3 [topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel]
  : I sat watching a little patch of coloured light creep towards the toes of my boots.
  : I held both feet still until the colour had passed like a warm tide.
  b : Was it worth waiting for?
  : My shoulders had come down a whole inch while I watched. I left lighter than I arrived.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wait for the sling to hang free. | Dry plank under that corner first.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Good light for turning out a pocket. | Even the rough coal shines in this light.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Black streak coming through my cuff again. | Drip quietly. I'm trying to count.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=pickled_herring
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A little vinegar would wake that bowl right up. | There's a fine silver shine in the pickle.
dlg resident.hub : There's a puzzle in my pocket and time left over for company.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you're welcome at my clean elbow.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Dark enough that the coal won't show even if I drop it.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : You can see both my paws. Out with your errand.
dlg resident.job [self.job=sailor] : I unload the ships. A steady pause before lifting saves trouble later.
dlg resident.job : I'm happiest when I can see a thing settled properly on the ground.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The news has landed here too. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I caught this. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. It has somebody else's prints all over it.
dlg resident.bye : Carry a chip of today's good luck away with you.

graft resident.hub
choice Can you tell a lucky coal by its shape? -> coal_print
node coal_print
say The first day they're all rough and ready to snag a lining. Rub one long enough and it begins to fit the place between your claws.
free
choice So the luck takes time? -> coal_print_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node coal_print_again
say My patience certainly does. The coal and I bring each other along.
choice Keep the smooth piece handy. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
